  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Support to ACEAC Bishops&apos; peace advocacy mission in the Great Lakes region</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project will seek to support the ACEAC Bishop&#x2019;s advocacy in the Great Lakes. The action will also aim to enable the ISPR/ACEAC to develop a strategic plan for the next five years (2023 - 2027) in order to map out the future through coherent programmes for more effective action in the service of peace and reconciliation in the African Great Lakes sub-region. All these actions will include :
1.	Conduct an update meeting between the delegate bishops of the Episcopal Conferences of Burundi, Congo and Rwanda; 
2.	Conduct joint advocacy targeting States and other key actors in the current crisis in the Great Lakes Region; 
3.	Organise an advocacy action in Burundi, whose Head of State is President of the EAC 
4.	Conducting advocacy with the Government of Kinshasa
5.	Identify and define the strategic axes of ISPR/ACEAC&#x2019; interventions; 
6.	Develop and validate the ISPR/ACEAC five-year strategic plan 2023-2027</narrative>
  </description>
